# Dedicated manifest: A46b runs a 533-token sequence (490 visual), so it needs
# a smaller per-device batch than the sweep default.
#
# NO EXTRACTION. It re-reads the s2d cache at five origins per window
# (data.visual_latent_anchors: 5), so VJEPA_CACHE_VER is the 8-frame s2d cache
# — NOT the 20-frame a24h cache that S2E and A46 read. Pointing this at a24h
# would load 20-latent ladders where the config expects 5 x 4, silently.
#
#   MANIFEST=configs/ablation/A46b.manifest N_VIS=5 \
#   VJEPA_CACHE_VER=vit_large_f8_s224_nonhrv_sp45 \
#   BATCH_SIZE=2 ACCUM=8 NPACKS=1 bash scripts/ablation_sweep.sh
#
# Run seed 42 alone first as a memory probe before releasing 43/44. If it OOMs,
# fall to 3 anchors (see A46b.yaml) rather than trimming the per-anchor budget,
# which would reintroduce the payload confound this arm exists to remove.
#
# Do NOT free vit_large_f8_s224_nonhrv_sp45 — under this route it is the input,
# not a scored control's leftovers. Nothing new is written, so quota is unchanged.
#
# ID   | MODE  | STAGE | MODEL_CFG             | SEEDS    | BASE
A46b  | train | s2e   | vision_chronos2_s2e   | 42,43,44 | uk_pv_s1_selfattn_s{seed}
